Title: The Tide Ledger
Credit: Table Read story-overview fixture (T7.30)
Author: Fixture
Draft date: 2026-07-17

# Planted overview signals: episode logline should capture Nora wanting to
# return the compass / pay a debt despite Cass; outline covers both scenes;
# beat sheet names a clear turn in each scene; synopsis is two paragraphs
# spoiling the dock payoff.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE COTTAGE - NIGHT

NORA turns a tarnished brass compass over in her hands, not looking at Cass.

NORA
Take it back when the tide turns. I'm not keeping what isn't mine.

CASS
You say that every winter, Nora. The tide's always turning.

NORA
(quiet)
Papa asked me to look after this house, not take from it. I need this back in your hands before I can call the debt paid.

EXT. HARBOR DOCK - DAWN

The tide has turned. NORA presses the brass compass into Cass's palm.

NORA
There. Paid in full. Papa can rest easy, and so can I.

CASS
(surprised, softening)
You didn't have to.

NORA
I did. That's the whole point of a promise.
